                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that North Carolina lacks jurisdiction because the court held that the mere sale of a defendant's products in a State does not permit the State to assert jurisdiction over the defendant's worldwide conduct."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "abe93e958e2165c1451e147edfaefd3c7f5bdaf65d7003d09cd68da99586ea20",
              "evidence_ids": [
